+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` looks at trades that closed within `lookback_period` in minutes (or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`), ordered from most recent to oldest.
+If the `max_consecutive_losses` most recent trades all closed at a loss with no winning trade in between, that pair will be locked for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`).
+
+Unlike `StoplossGuard`, this does not care about the exit reason - any trade closed at a loss counts towards the streak, and a single winning (or break-even) trade resets it.
+
+This applies across all pairs, unless `only_per_pair` is set to true, which will then only look at one pair at a time. To get an independent bot-wide streak check with its own threshold and cool-down, add a second `MaxConsecutiveLosses` entry without `only_per_pair` set.
+
+The below example stops trading a pair for 12 candles after 3 consecutive losing trades within the last 24 candles.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 24,
+            "max_consecutive_losses": 3,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 12,
+            "only_per_pair": False
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
 ### Full example of Protections
 
 All protections can be combined at will, also with different parameters, creating a increasing wall for under-performing pairs.
