+"IProtection::MaxConsecutiveLosses()":
+  location: max_consecutive_losses.py
+  annotations: |
+    Locks trading (globally, or per-pair unless `only_per_pair` is set) once the most recent
+    closed trades within the lookback window form an unbroken losing streak of at least
+    `max_consecutive_losses` trades. Unlike StoplossGuard/LowProfitPairs, the trigger is purely
+    the unbroken streak of consecutive losses (by close_profit < 0), not exit reason or total
+    profit; the streak breaks on the first non-losing trade walking back from the most recent
+    close. One of several concrete handlers in this cell; see `extension_point`.
